Package: polycall
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: program-first cross-language runtime - command-line tool
 PolyCall routes a call made of a service name, an operation name and a
 JSON input to whichever process registered that operation, over one wire
 protocol (polycall_rpc v1), so callers written in any language reach the
 same typed operation and get the same typed result or structured error.
 .
 This package provides the polycall command. It starts the runtime in the
 foreground or as a daemon, queries and stops a running instance over its
 control channel, invokes registered operations, loads operation plugins,
 validates and migrates configuration, and records GUID and timestamp
 correlated telemetry events.

Package: libpolycall1
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: program-first cross-language runtime - shared library
 PolyCall routes a call made of a service name, an operation name and a
 JSON input to whichever process registered that operation, over one wire
 protocol (polycall_rpc v1), so callers written in any language reach the
 same typed operation and get the same typed result or structured error.
 .
 This package contains the shared library implementing the runtime,
 typed configuration model, provider host and telemetry C API.

Package: libpolycall-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libpolycall1 (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends},
Description: program-first cross-language runtime - development files
 PolyCall routes a call made of a service name, an operation name and a
 JSON input to whichever process registered that operation, over one wire
 protocol (polycall_rpc v1), so callers written in any language reach the
 same typed operation and get the same typed result or structured error.
 .
 This package contains the C headers, the static library, the shared
 library symlink and the CMake package configuration (find_package
 polycall, targets polycall::polycall_shared and polycall::polycall_static)
 needed to build programs and operation plugins against libpolycall.
